"""B18 stage 1: the controls the live read did not reach, read from the source by hand.

The live read brings up the windows it can reach on one test character. Some controls exist only in a state that
character is not in (an Ancestor's after-roll gifts, the Library's book reader, the wizard's later screens, the PDF
window). static_scan.py finds where each is created; this file says what each one is, because many labels are built at
runtime. Every entry names the source file by a slug and the line static_scan.py reported, so a changed source line shows
up as an entry that no longer matches.

Fields: label (as written), spoken (the aria-label or the text a screen reader gets; "=" means the label itself),
title, where, mode ('Manage', 'Play', 'Both' or 'unknown'), group (a jobs.py group, or '' to let jobs.py decide), note.
An entry with "rows" makes several rows from one source line. "drop" marks a hit that is not a control.
"""

DROP_REASONS = {
    'file download': 'an anchor made only to save a file; it is never shown',
    'click filter': 'a selector inside a click handler, not a control',
    'live': 'the same control is already in the live read',
    'described': 'described by another entry for the same function',
    'not a control': 'code that looks for controls, or a module comment',
}

